1
00:00:00,583 --> 00:00:02,208
Talks without a deal.

2
00:00:02,292 --> 00:00:04,625
An election without a majority.

3
00:00:04,708 --> 00:00:07,917
Families escaping through a temporary ceasefire.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,167
And an AI boom facing an expensive question:

5
00:00:11,167 --> 00:00:13,333
when does the spending pay off?

6
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,250
Five stories. One turbulent week.

7
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:18,542
This is the world in anime.

8
00:00:19,792 --> 00:00:25,000
We start in the Gulf, where diplomacy continued under the threat of renewed strikes.

9
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:30,583
On Sunday, Iranian negotiators were in Doha for talks with Qatari mediators,

10
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:35,583
seeking a way to end the war involving Iran, the United States and Israel.

11
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:40,833
Iran’s foreign minister described a proposal that could reopen the Strait of Hormuz

12
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:44,792
within two days of a possible agreement with Washington.

13
00:00:45,042 --> 00:00:48,333
But he said no final agreement had been reached.

14
00:00:48,583 --> 00:00:52,250
The shipping route remains central to the negotiations.

15
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:57,583
For now, the diplomatic breakthrough is still a possibility—not an announced outcome.

16
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:03,708
In Israel, the votes are counted. Forming a government is the next battle.

17
00:01:03,792 --> 00:01:08,833
Results released on Friday gave Benjamin Netanyahu’s bloc fifty-three seats.

18
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,833
The main opposition bloc took forty-eight.

19
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,542
Arab-led parties held nineteen.

20
00:01:14,792 --> 00:01:18,542
For an outright majority, the target is sixty-one seats

21
00:01:18,542 --> 00:01:21,500
in the one-hundred-and-twenty-seat parliament.

22
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,667
Netanyahu remains prime minister while parties try to build a coalition.

23
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:31,583
Those nineteen seats do not automatically belong to either main bloc.

24
00:01:31,667 --> 00:01:33,708
The election is over.

25
00:01:33,792 --> 00:01:38,167
The struggle to turn votes into a governing majority continues.

26
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:43,917
Now to Ukraine, where this week brought a narrow opening for civilians.

27
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:50,042
On Saturday, evacuees from Russian-occupied Oleshky reached Ukrainian-held territory

28
00:01:50,042 --> 00:01:52,292
and reunited with relatives.

29
00:01:52,375 --> 00:01:55,417
Their route ran through Russia and Belarus,

30
00:01:55,417 --> 00:01:59,750
under a local ceasefire that also allowed humanitarian aid.

31
00:01:59,833 --> 00:02:04,375
That pause began on Tuesday and was scheduled to end on Sunday evening.

32
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:06,542
It covered a limited area.

33
00:02:06,625 --> 00:02:11,375
Fighting continued elsewhere in Ukraine. The wider war went on.

34
00:02:11,792 --> 00:02:16,042
But for families arriving at the border, the week brought something immediate:

35
00:02:16,125 --> 00:02:19,125
getting out, reaching safety, finding each other.

36
00:02:22,125 --> 00:02:25,167
In France, the pressure moved onto the streets.

37
00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:29,583
Saturday brought a third consecutive weekend of demonstrations

38
00:02:29,583 --> 00:02:32,500
over living costs and education.

39
00:02:32,583 --> 00:02:38,167
Authorities estimated three-hundred-and-twenty-thousand participants across the country.

40
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:40,750
Organizers put the number higher.

41
00:02:40,917 --> 00:02:43,083
Most people marched peacefully.

42
00:02:43,417 --> 00:02:48,417
Later clashes involving smaller groups broke out in Paris and other cities.

43
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:53,708
The movement’s demands have broadened to include civil liberties and the right to protest.

44
00:02:53,792 --> 00:02:56,042
The crowds filled the streets.

45
00:02:56,125 --> 00:03:00,292
The political questions behind the protests remained unresolved.

46
00:03:01,542 --> 00:03:06,208
Across the Atlantic, confidence came under pressure on the trading screens.

47
00:03:06,292 --> 00:03:10,875
On Friday, the S and P five hundred fell one-point-eight percent.

48
00:03:11,125 --> 00:03:14,583
The Nasdaq Composite dropped two-point-nine percent.

49
00:03:14,833 --> 00:03:18,792
Technology shares led the sell-off as disappointing earnings

50
00:03:18,792 --> 00:03:23,542
and concerns about huge AI investments unsettled investors.

51
00:03:23,625 --> 00:03:26,542
The question is becoming harder to dodge:

52
00:03:26,542 --> 00:03:30,333
how much of that spending will turn into financial returns?

53
00:03:30,583 --> 00:03:34,167
The AI race carries enormous expectations.

54
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:37,208
This week, Wall Street delivered a reminder

55
00:03:37,208 --> 00:03:41,333
that expectations still have to survive an earnings report.

56
00:03:42,833 --> 00:03:45,375
And one more countdown is running.

57
00:03:45,542 --> 00:03:50,250
On Tuesday, November third, Americans vote in the midterm elections,

58
00:03:50,250 --> 00:03:52,750
with control of Congress at stake.

59
00:03:52,833 --> 00:03:55,083
That result is still ahead.

60
00:03:55,333 --> 00:03:59,250
Talks continue. Coalitions remain unresolved.

61
00:03:59,333 --> 00:04:01,750
Another major vote approaches.

62
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:06,042
This was the week ending November first, twenty twenty-six.

63
00:04:06,292 --> 00:04:08,833
The next chapter is still open.
